{
  "_comment": [
    "One channel's worth of conversation, for `starcord --replay` and for the",
    "chat panel's snapshots. Synthetic, like everything else in testdata: no",
    "account was recorded from, and a fixture that pretends to be a recording",
    "is worse than one that says it is not.",
    "",
    "Ids follow ready.json's conventions -- 1000000000000000NN for users,",
    "2000000000000000NN for guild things, 5000000000000000NN for messages,",
    "6000000000000000NN for attachments, 7000000000000000NN for emoji -- so",
    "the three files can be read side by side.",
    "",
    "It exists to carry one of each thing the renderer has to get right: a",
    "group of three from the same person, a reply, reactions (one of them",
    "this account's own), a fenced code block, a spoiler, an inline image, a",
    "link-preview card, a gifv, a system message, a mention of the reader, and",
    "a day boundary in the middle so the date divider is drawn. `older` is the",
    "page `LoadOlder` answers with, which is what proves the view does not",
    "jump when history arrives above it."
  ],
